Experiment: Network Traffic Analysis using NetworkMiner (Kali Linux)
🎯 Aim

To capture and analyze network traffic using tcpdump and NetworkMiner in Kali Linux.

🎯 Objectives
To understand network traffic analysis
To capture live network traffic using tcpdump
To analyze .pcap files using NetworkMiner
To identify hosts, sessions, and DNS activity
To extract files, images, and credentials (if available)
🧠 Concept (Short for Viva)

Network Traffic Analysis involves monitoring and inspecting packets flowing through a network.

tcpdump → captures network packets
NetworkMiner → analyzes captured packets (PCAP files)
NetworkMiner is a passive tool (does not generate traffic)
⚙️ Tools Used
6
tcpdump (for packet capture)
NetworkMiner (for analysis)
🧾 Requirements
Kali Linux
NetworkMiner installed
Internet connection
🪜 Procedure (Step-by-Step)
🔹 Step 1: Identify Network Interface
ip a

👉 Interface identified: eth0

🔹 Step 2: Capture Network Traffic using tcpdump
sudo tcpdump -i eth0 -w test.pcap
Tool starts capturing packets
🔹 Step 3: Generate Network Traffic
Open browser
Visit:
http://example.com
http://neverssl.com

👉 (Use HTTP for visible data)

🔹 Step 4: Stop Capture

Press:

Ctrl + C

👉 Packets captured successfully

🔹 Step 5: Launch NetworkMiner
mono NetworkMiner.exe
🔹 Step 6: Load PCAP File
Click File → Open
Select:
test.pcap
🔹 Step 7: Analyze Hosts
Open Hosts Tab
View:
Source IP
Destination IP
🔹 Step 8: Analyze DNS Activity
Observe domains accessed
Example:
example.com
neverssl.com
🔹 Step 9: Analyze Files and Images
Open Files Tab → extracted files
Open Images Tab → transferred images
🔹 Step 10: Check Credentials
Open Credentials Tab
Observe if any username/password present
👀 Observations
Network traffic was successfully captured using tcpdump
Multiple hosts were identified in the Hosts tab
DNS queries revealed accessed websites
Limited files and images were extracted
No credentials were found due to encrypted traffic
Communication between client and server was observed
✅ Result

The network traffic was successfully captured using tcpdump and analyzed using NetworkMiner. Important artifacts such as hosts and DNS queries were identified, demonstrating the effectiveness of network traffic analysis in monitoring and investigating network activities.
